          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "Course Description",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 103.624146,
          "r": 182.18001,
          "b": 108.859985,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "ENME 431 presents the major fluid systems used in nuclear reactor power plants, including",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 130.14417,
          "r": 514.84686,
          "b": 135.38,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "the bases for the designs of these systems.  The emphasis is on auxiliary and safety systems;",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 143.34418,
          "r": 516.4252,
          "b": 148.58002,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, primary coolant systems are also discussed.  Systems used in existing nuclear",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 156.54419,
          "r": 494.76947,
          "b": 161.78003,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "power plants are presented, as well as proposed systems for advanced nuclear power plant",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 169.74414,
          "r": 507.34744,
          "b": 174.97998,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "concepts.  Major components used in nuclear reactor fluid systems (pumps, valves and heat",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 183.06415,
          "r": 513.37225,
          "b": 188.29999,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "exchangers) are discussed.  In addition, nuclear reactor safety, including regulatory",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 196.26416,
          "r": 474.9522,
          "b": 201.5,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
          "text": "requirements and safety analysis, are discussed.",
          "l": 90.024,
          "t": 209.46417,
          "r": 312.29,
          "b": 214.70001,
          "origin": "PdfTextLayer"
        },
        {
